# AGENT BEHAVIOR RULES

## 1. Bulk Edits & Execution Limits
- NEVER open and edit HTML/CSS files individually if updating 2+ files.
- ALWAYS write a single Python script (using regex or string replacement) to apply edits across all `.html` files in one batch.
- Execute the script using Bash/PowerShell, verify the file outputs, and delete the script when finished.
- DO NOT spawn background subagents (`Agent(...)` or `DefineSubagent`) unless explicitly instructed. Perform all tasks directly in the main thread.

## 2. Token & Quota Management
- Stop and ask before reading files greater than 100 lines if only minor variable/CSS tweaks are needed.
- Clear context after completing major structural milestones.

## 3. Design System ("Technical Flora" - Dark Mode)
- Primary BG: `#0A120D` (Deep Dark Green)
- Card BG: `#132217` (Slightly Lighter Dark Green)
- Text Main: `#E2E8F0` (Light Slate)
- Text Muted: `#94A3B8`
- Accents: `#38A169` (Forest Sage), `#4ADE80` (Active Green)
- Borders: `#1E3F20` (1px solid)
- Typography: Inter (body), JetBrains Mono (tech spec tags)

## 4. Writing Style
- Tone: Genuine, technical, concise, first-person ("I").
- Avoid AI buzzwords, promotional fluff, or sentences formatted as "From [X] to [Y], [Z]".
- Focus on hardware specs, concrete deliverables, measurements, and engineering tradeoffs.